    "updated_at": "2022-06-07T07:57:39Z",
    "body": "> Regardless, this use case should be satisfied soon anyways, since we're hoping to allow [`move()`](https://github.com/whatwg/fs/pull/10) to support moving files and directories from the sandboxed file system to a folder of the user's choice.\r\n\r\nTIL that this is on the roadmap. We should then probably update [this section](https://github.com/WICG/file-system-access/blob/main/AccessHandle.md#:~:text=Although%20this%20proposal%20is%20the%20successor%20%22in%20spirit%22%20to%20the%20Storage%20Foundation%20API%2C%20the%20two%20APIs%20operate%20on%20entirely%20different%20sets%20of%20files.%20There%20exists%20no%20way%20of%20accessing%20a%20file%20stored%20through%20Storage%20Foundation%20API%20using%20the%20Origin%20Private%20File%20System%2C%20and%20vice%20versa.) of the AccessHandle explainer and set expectations that OPFS→regular FS is a flow we want to enable.\r\n\r\n",
